WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.001
20 years ago on

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:01.501
this night

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:01.801
I anchored

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.536
my first broadcast in 360

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.938
and it's been 31 years

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.339
since I shot my first story.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.173
And since then I've worked

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.408
in more than 70 countries

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.509
around the world

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.110
seeing things

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.878
I could never have imagined and spoken

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.279
to extraordinary people, often

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.014
in very dangerous

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.915
and difficult circumstances.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.917
It has been an incredible honor

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:18.785
to do this job

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:19.319
and to work

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.420
with such a talented team

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.554
of dedicated journalists

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.223
here at CNN tonight

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.858
because it is the actual anniversary.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:25.725
We wanted to take some time

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.393
and pull together

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.660
some of the most memorable moments

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.162
from the last 20 years,

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.163
starting with this night.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.132
20 years ago,

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.701
Live from the CNN

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.736
Broadcast Center in New York,

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.605
this is Anderson Cooper.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:39.539
360

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.641
and a good evening to you.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:42.275
Thanks for joining us.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:42.976
I'm Anderson Cooper.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.177
Welcome to our debut hour.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:45.512
We're following a number of developments

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.179
for you tonight.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:46.913
Tonight from Port

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.181
au Prince in Cairo,

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.682
a day of dramatic developments.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.950
We are in the city of Manaus,

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:51.518
which is really in

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:52.719
the heart of the Amazon.

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.521
We are live tonight from Baghdad,

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.856
live in New Orleans.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.325
There is desperation

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.326
and there is danger

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.228
in the city of New Orleans tonight.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.464
And what you are about to see in

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.231
this next hour

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:06.399
is going to shock you

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.801
that this is taking place

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.636
in the United States of America

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.404
in this day and age,

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.173
people stuck in their homes right now.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.041
No electricity, no ice,

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.476
nothing cool to drink.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:17.877
They don't know where to go.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.112
They don't know what to do

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:19.779
and they don't

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.081
really have any information.

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:22.248
I want to thank Senator

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.417
Frist and Senator Reid

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.853
for their extraordinary efforts Anderson.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.521
Tonight, I don't know if you've heard

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.223
maybe you all have announced it,

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.624
but Congress is going to

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.959
an unprecedented session

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.661
to pass a $10 billion

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:37.363
supplemental bill tonight to keep FEMA

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.399
across, up and operating.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.034
Excuse me, Senator.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:41.935
I'm sorry for interrupting.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:42.869
I haven't heard that

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.171
because for the last four days,

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.773
I've been seeing dead bodies

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.842
in the streets here in Mississippi.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.743
And to listen to politicians

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:51.744
thanking each other

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:54.013
and complimenting each other.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:54.848
You know, I got to tell you,

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:55.782
there are a lot of people here

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:56.983
who are very upset

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.219
and very angry and very frustrated.

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.321
And when they hear politicians slap,

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.523
you know, thanking one another,

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:04.057
it just

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:04.491
you know, it

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.493
kind of cuts up the wrong way right now.

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:07.760
Because literally,

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.762
there was a body on the streets

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:12.065
of this town yesterday

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.800
being eaten by rats

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.601
because this woman

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.602
had been laying in the street

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.970
for for 48 hours

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.371
and there's not enough facilities

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.506
to take her up.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:19.772
Do you

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.541
do you get the anger that is out here?

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:23.042
Good evening.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.211
I'm Anderson Cooper in Marathi, Niger.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.813
Starving in plain sight.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.581
The food crisis in Niger.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.316
That's exactly what is happening here.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.017
A crisis,

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:31.751
a food shortage,

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:32.552
the likes of which

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.921
this country has rarely seen

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.256
the level of everyday

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.724
violence here in the Democratic

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:38.558
Republic of Congo

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.126
has been simply unfathomable

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.761
over the last several years.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.463
Guns and machetes, of course, are common.

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:45.498
But the most ruthless, ruthless weapon

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.067
that has been used here is rape here.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:48.935
But there are injured

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:49.903
people in the neighborhood

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:50.403
just point

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.371
fingers and say,

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:52.472
you are raped woman

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.741
and you are infected with AIDS.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:55.475
She and her children

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:56.809
have been living here in Goma

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.111
for the last five months.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.012
Angela would like to be able

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.280
to return to her home village,

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.582
but that's simply impossible.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.516
The men who raped her

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.951
are likely still living in the area.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.752
They of course, have never

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:06.719
been brought to justice.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:08.288
We're on

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.889
a way to see General Laurent Nkunda.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:10.924
He's a rebel commander

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.392
with several thousand troops.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:12.825
So far, he's

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.761
been unwilling to give up his weapons.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.496
He's been accused of a host of war crimes

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:17.797
and human rights violations.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.465
His troops are known to have looted

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.833
villages, raped women.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.901
He's been accused

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.403
of ordering the summary executions

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.071
of dozens of prisoners

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.406
the Congolese government issued

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.474
an international arrest warrant for him,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.809
but so far, it seems no one's

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.979
been able or willing to apprehend him.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:34.147
When the U.S.

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.448
military helicopter

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.549
headed toward a forward

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.383
operating base

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.651
in eastern Afghanistan

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.587
along the Pakistan border.

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:41.287
We're actually now

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.655
just getting some fire.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.324
Some rockets have been fired

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:45.291
We're coming to you tonight

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.360
live from Gaza City, where today

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.128
we have seen continued violence.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:52.031
Also, two media centers being closed

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.136
That was a rather large explosion.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.671
We've come to Iraq this week,

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.640
along with a platoon of CNN producers

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.741
and correspondents

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.743
to look at exactly what is happening here

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:06.045
on the military and the political fronts.

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:07.280
Before we go on this journey,

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.748
we're giving warnings about what to do

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.283
if we're hit by an IED,

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.318
by grenades or by small arms fire.

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:13.653
This security situation

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.555
where we are has changed somewhat

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:16.990
in the last 30 minutes or so.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:17.624
We've been advised

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:19.659
to actually turn off our lights,

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.261
get down on the floor

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.061
and try to barricade

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.063
ourselves in the area that we're in.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.331
So that's what

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.033
that's why we're doing this program

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:27.734
like this tonight.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:28.735
It's not going to look very good

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:29.402
over the next hour.

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:30.370
But I hope you bear with us,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.572
because what has happened today in Egypt

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:34.440
and on these streets

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.476
has been nothing short of extraordinary.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:38.911
My cameraman, Neil Holdsworth

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.313
and my producer, Marianne Fox

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.781
and I were heading toward

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:42.749
Liberation Square

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.183
in order to report on both sides

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.652
of that protest.

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:47.086
Suddenly, a man jumped out of the crowd

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:49.622
and tried to grab Neil's camera.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:52.659
That's when all hell broke loose

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.328
people started throwing punches,

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:58.097
pushing us around, screaming.

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.768
We immediately decided to turn around

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:03.603
and try to get to a safe location.

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.672
Several Egyptian men helped us,

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.006
but still the crowd followed,

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.041
throwing punches.

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:08.508
That man

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:10.810
there had a knife in his hand and

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.080
he

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:20.520
kept joining in, trying to punch us.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.954
We only had about a block left to go

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:22.955
when another guy came up

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.824
and punched me in the head.

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:28.561
I've been hit now

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.396
like ten times

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:32.432
Yep.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:35.535
Egyptian soldiers

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:37.036
use it for

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:39.372
soldiers who are doing nothing

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:46.746
on the one.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:51.017
Finally, we reached a safe location, but.

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:52.452
And

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:54.787
we go

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:59.392
with the first live

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:01.661
here's Leah.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.263
All we were trying to do today

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:04.864
was report

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:07.767
on both sides of this conflict.

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.370
We're saying that there's two teams now

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.471
that are inside the mine.

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:13.940
They've made their way about 4800 feet

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:15.475
towards the trapped workers.

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:16.242
In a minute. Wait a minute.

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:17.377
Charlie. Charlie.

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:19.445
We got to come back come back to us.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:20.680
The rope is there. All.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.681
Where do I come here?

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:22.949
What's happening?

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:23.883
There's only one.

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.985
There's only one. Made it out alive.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.053
You were inside the church?

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:28.621
We were inside the church. And.

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.423
And you said there's fierce fighting now.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:30.656
Yeah.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.024
People are screaming. You're a liar.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:32.992
You've lied to us.

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:34.560
We come over here, please.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.596
And misinformation, and it's awful.

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:37.497
And you.

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:39.098
You kids were in the church, too? Yeah.

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:39.999
And you heard this?

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:41.634
Yeah. We tried to run away.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:42.101
We.

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:43.169
I took the kids,

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:44.337
and we ran out of the church

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:45.805
as fast as we can.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:46.773
I can hear yelling

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:48.307
now over the screaming and yelling,

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:50.176
and the police are in a big draw,

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:51.477
and I don't know how

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:53.246
something like this can happen.

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:55.581
This is CNN breaking news

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.849
tonight from Port au Prince.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:58.951
Haiti, the epicenter of this

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:01.387
horrible earthquake which has struck here

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:03.256
more than 24 hours ago.

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:04.557
Our correspondents have fanned out

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.826
throughout the port of Port City of Port

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:08.594
au Prince throughout this day,

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:09.128
bringing you

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:10.296
the latest information

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:12.165
as we have seen it through our eyes

00:07:12.165 --> 00:07:13.232
and as the Haitian people

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.534
are experiencing it

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:15.268
every minute,

00:07:15.268 --> 00:07:17.103
wherever you are watching this broadcast

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:17.804
throughout the world,

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:19.839
I hope you can hug a loved one close

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:21.707
and thank God that you are not in Port

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:22.742
au Prince tonight.

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:23.209
Monley

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:25.278
Alisa was brought to General Hospital

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:26.379
by his uncle

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:27.346
who says he found him

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:28.614
in the rubble alive.

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:30.750
After nearly eight days,

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.418
Monley was covered in dust,

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:33.953
weak and limp.

00:07:33.953 --> 00:07:35.988
A doctor and a nurse quickly gave him.

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:38.691
And I've got them because as you said,

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:42.528
Lisa, you feel good

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:45.064
He's already looking better

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:45.898
since he's gotten here.

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:47.266
You might have some complications.

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:48.334
Maybe he's

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:50.203
got a very good chance of survival.

00:07:50.203 --> 00:07:52.138
And joining us now is Monley.

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:53.439
We're very happy to have him here.

00:07:53.439 --> 00:07:54.774
And registered nurse

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:55.608
Gabriella McAdoo,

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:56.809
who is from Stanford

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:57.844
Hospital in California.

00:07:57.844 --> 00:07:59.011
But when I first saw him this morning,

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:01.113
I didn't recognize the moment he's here.

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:02.081
He's hydrated now.

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:03.082
And when we first got him,

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:04.050
he was dehydrated.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.852
So we gave him some fluids.

00:08:05.852 --> 00:08:08.821
And after eating and drinking, he just

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:11.657
this process is great.

00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:14.694
2 hours ago or so, when when

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:16.929
when you guys heard distinctive tapping.

00:08:17.263 --> 00:08:17.930
Is it possible

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.299
that was just ambient noise?

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:20.933
It very well

00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:22.935
could have been the other possibility

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:24.670
is that a person expires

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.005
at the tap at one point

00:08:26.005 --> 00:08:27.406
and then they're no longer able to.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:28.474
Mr. True.

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:29.909
This is we're four days into it

00:08:29.909 --> 00:08:31.377
without food or water,

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:32.945
and we're talking about possibly

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:33.846
a ten year old girl.

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:36.182
